.\" Title: vrl-spawn-in
.\" Author: vrl contributors
.\" Manual section: 1
.\"
.TH VRL\-SPAWN\-IN 1 "2025" "vrl" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
vrl\-spawn\-in \- spawn a new command inside a running vrl instance

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vrl
\fBspawn\-in\fR \fIPID\fR \fICMD\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]

.SH DESCRIPTION
Spawn a new command inside an already-running vrl instance. The new command gets its own virtual terminal (VTTY) with independent scrollback, and is added to the instance's command list visible via \fBvrl list\fR.

Connects to the target instance's UDS control socket at \fB~/.local/share/vrl/control\-{pid}.sock\fR and sends the spawn request.

The spawned command uses the instance's default VTTY settings (rows, cols, TERM value) unless overridden in the configuration. Environment variables from the config are passed to the new command.

This is the UDS equivalent of vrunner's \fBvrunner spawn\fR command.

.SH ARGUMENTS

.TP
.B PID
OS process ID of the target vrl instance.

.TP
.B CMD
The command to run (e.g., \fBhtop\fR, \fBvim\fR, \fB./my-script.sh\fR).

.TP
.B ARGS...
Additional arguments to pass to the command.

.SH EXAMPLES

.PP
Spawn htop in a running instance:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrl spawn\-in 12345 htop\fR
Spawned command cmd_abc (PID 5678) in instance 12345
.fi
.RE

.PP
Spawn a script with arguments:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrl spawn\-in 12345 ./build.sh \-\-release \-\-verbose\fR
Spawned command cmd_def (PID 5679) in instance 12345
.fi
.RE

.PP
Spawn vim to edit a file:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrl spawn\-in 12345 vim /path/to/file.rs\fR
Spawned command cmd_ghi (PID 5680) in instance 12345
.fi
.RE

.SH EXIT STATUS

.TP
.B 0
Command spawned successfully.

.TP
.B 1
Error (instance not found, spawn failed, etc.).

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vrl (1),
.BR vrl\-list (1),
.BR vrl\-kill (1),
.BR vrl\-freeze (1)
